{
  "$comment": [
    "Frozen inventory of the upstream custom-element tag names lyra-ui's migration tables are",
    "measured against. Recorded from the published sources at the versions below; regenerate",
    "deliberately when bumping a version, never silently.",
    "",
    "webawesome.free  -- every tag Web Awesome's open-source package registers via @customElement.",
    "webawesome.pro   -- the Pro-tier tags, which ship no public source. Enumerated from Web",
    "                    Awesome's own docs; these are the components lyra-ui exists to reimplement,",
    "                    so they count toward migration coverage exactly like the free ones.",
    "shoelace         -- every tag Shoelace registers via `.define('sl-*')`.",
    "",
    "noCounterpart    -- upstream tags lyra-ui deliberately does not mirror. Each needs a reason;",
    "                    the coverage gate treats an unlisted, unmapped tag as a failure.",
    "",
    "attributeRenames -- every upstream attribute whose lyra spelling differs, or that was",
    "                    deliberately kept identical after a polarity fix. The gate fails when a",
    "                    pair disagrees on polarity (`light-dismiss` vs `no-light-dismiss`,",
    "                    `with-summary` vs `hide-summary`): a rename that flips a boolean's sense",
    "                    still parses, so nothing errors and the component just behaves the other",
    "                    way round.",
    "",
    "unaliasedEvents  -- upstream events lyra-ui deliberately does not dispatch under their",
    "                    migrated name, keyed `\"<upstream-tag> <event>\"`. The gate requires every",
    "                    event a mapped upstream tag dispatches to land on an event the Lyra",
    "                    target actually dispatches, because a renamed mirrored event is the",
    "                    quietest parity break there is: the markup still parses, the codemod",
    "                    still reports success, and the consumer's listener just never fires.",
    "                    An entry whose event has since been aliased is reported as stale, so",
    "                    this list can never quietly outlive its reason. Empty is the goal.",
    "",
    "runtimeEventCancelability -- black-box observations used only when an exact pinned package's",
    "                    published manifest omits cancelability. Every record covers the named",
    "                    public transition paths and becomes stale on an artifact or manifest",
    "                    change; it is comparison evidence, never an executable rewrite.",
    "",
    "runtimeMethodEdgeSemantics -- artifact-bound black-box observations for public method edge",
    "                    cases whose return behavior is absent from the published manifest. Each",
    "                    case records only public inputs/outcomes and becomes stale when the exact",
    "                    package, method signature, or reviewed case changes."
  ],
  "webawesome": {
    "version": "3.11.0",
